488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (Unlike GitHub and Slack, BLT exposes a REST API rather than webhook based event delivery. The system integrates BLT signals by periodically polling endpoints such as /bugs and /hunts, which provide structured data on bug reports, contributor activity, and ongoing hunts. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (A last_seen_id mechanism ensures that only newly created or updated records are processed, preventing duplication across polling cycles. Retrieved records are transformed into the normalized Event schema, allowing BLT activity to be treated identically to GitHub and Slack events within the pipeline.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (This adapter is isolated from the core ingestion layer and is explicitly additive temporary BLT API failures do not impact realtime processing of GitHub or Slack events.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
